G2675.def:
**κατ-αρτίζω **
[in LXX chiefly in Ps ([[Psa.8.2|Psa.8:2]] al.; כּוּן, etc.) and Ezra (כְּלַל) ;]
to render ἄρτιος, i.e. fit, complete;
(a) **to mend, repair**: [[Mat.4.21|Mat.4:21]], [[Mrk.1.19|Mrk.1:19]];
(b) **to furnish completely, complete, equip, prepare**: pass., [[Luk.6.40|Luk.6:40]], [[Rom.9.22|Rom.9:22]], [[Heb.11.3|Heb.11:3]]; mid., [[Mat.21.16|Mat.21:16]] (LXX), [[Heb.10.5|Heb.10:5]] (LXX);
(with) **in ethical sense, to prepare, complete, perfect**: [[Gal.6.1|Gal.6:1]] (EV, restore), [[1Pe.5.10|1Pe.5:10]] pass., [[1Co.1.10|1Co.1:10]] (Field, _Notes_, 167), [[2Co.13.11|2Co.13:11]], [[Heb.13.21|Heb.13:21]] (cf. προ-καταρτίζω).†
(AS)

G2634.def:
**κατα-κυριεύω **
[in LXX: [[Gen.1.28|Gen.1:28]] (כָּבַשׁ), [[Psa.110.2|Psa.110:2]] [[Sir.17.4|Sir.17:4]], al. ;]
**to gain or exercise dominion **(over);
(a) absol. (Arist.);
(b) with genitive (Arist., al.): [[Mat.20.25|Mat.20:25]], [[Mrk.10.42|Mrk.10:42]], [[Act.19.16|Act.19:16]], [[1Pe.5.3|1Pe.5:3]].†
_SYN._: (κατεξουσιάζω) (see Swete, _Mk._, l.with) (AS)
